From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhengping Zhang <zhengping.zhang@airoha.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:13:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] phy: airoha: fix AN7583 USB SerDes mode setup

Select USB on the underlying SerDes before U3 calibration rather than
relying on the bootloader mux state. The USB core sets the host mode
after PHY initialization, which is too late to select the calibration
path.

Accept USB_HOST, USB_DEVICE and USB_OTG in the U3 PHY and SCU SerDes
callbacks and map them to the USB mux selection. This permits the USB
core host-mode fallback and keeps the two mode handlers consistent.

Keep these downstream fixes separate from the upstream PHY and SCU
backports so they remain visible when those patches are refreshed.

Signed-off-by: Zhengping Zhang <zhengping.zhang@airoha.com>
---
 drivers/clk/clk-en7523.c            |    6 ++++++
 drivers/phy/airoha/phy-an7583-usb.c |   10 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/clk/clk-en7523.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clk-en7523.c
@@ -1214,6 +1214,9 @@ static int en7581_serdes_phy_set_mode(st
 		mask = REG_SSUSB_HSGMII_SEL_MASK;
 
 		if (mode != PHY_MODE_ETHERNET &&
+		    mode != PHY_MODE_USB_HOST &&
+		    mode != PHY_MODE_USB_DEVICE &&
+		    mode != PHY_MODE_USB_OTG &&
 		    mode != PHY_MODE_USB_DEVICE_SS)
 			return -EINVAL;
 
@@ -1228,6 +1231,9 @@ static int en7581_serdes_phy_set_mode(st
 		mask = REG_USB_PCIE_SEL_MASK;
 
 		if (mode != PHY_MODE_PCIE &&
+		    mode != PHY_MODE_USB_HOST &&
+		    mode != PHY_MODE_USB_DEVICE &&
+		    mode != PHY_MODE_USB_OTG &&
 		    mode != PHY_MODE_USB_DEVICE_SS)
 			return -EINVAL;
 
--- a/drivers/phy/airoha/phy-an7583-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/airoha/phy-an7583-usb.c
@@ -867,8 +867,14 @@ static void an7583_usb_phy_kband_calibra
 
 static int an7583_usb_phy_u3_init(struct phy *phy)
 {
+	struct an7583_usb_phy_instance *instance = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
 	struct an7583_usb_phy_priv *priv;
 	struct device *dev;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = phy_set_mode_ext(instance->serdes_phy, PHY_MODE_USB_DEVICE_SS, 0);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	dev = phy->dev.parent;
 	priv = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
@@ -1708,8 +1714,10 @@ static int an7583_usb_phy_u3_set_mode(st
 		    submode != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_1000BASEX &&
 		    submode != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX)
 			return -EOPNOTSUPP;
-
 		break;
+	case PHY_MODE_USB_HOST:
+	case PHY_MODE_USB_DEVICE:
+	case PHY_MODE_USB_OTG:
 	case PHY_MODE_USB_DEVICE_SS:
 		break;
 	default:
